"""Manual coding of the 66 SGLang kernel-performance revert rows of the B1 census.

The codebook is the one in coding.py, with three more causes that only SGLang needs:
  KERNEL  a defect inside the kernel code (own, vendored or third-party)
  API     a caller and a callee disagree: inside the PR, or between sglang and the separately
          released sgl-kernel package
  PERFREG the change is slower on another configuration, or a wrong measurement showed the gain
and with two wider definitions:
  DEP     a dependency version or behavior: not released, not pinned, or not as documented
  BUILD   also a platform-specific path that is not guarded and breaks another platform at run time
symptom adds "perf". warpdrf adds "direct": a bounds, race or launch-condition defect in a Triton
kernel or at its call site, which warpDRF checks (expected from the code; warpDRF was not run).

One row per census revert row. `pr` is the reverted PR. Rows that the census gives no target
have `rollback` (the census revert PR) and the target that the reading found, or pr=None.
The PR numbers in `reland` and `detail` are SGLang PRs.
"""

